        "text": "In order to be successful in trading and investing, you need to understand financial markets, market trends, and cycles. Let's dive into exactly what they are. A market is simply where buyers and sellers meet to trade. Going to the grocery store to buy apples is an example of a market. The price you pay for something in a market is dependent on the balance of supply from sellers and demand from buyers. If the grocery store is struggling to supply apples, but consumers want to purchase lots of them, the price will increase. If there is no demand for apples but a huge supply, the price will decrease. Anywhere supply meets demand, a market exists. Financial markets take the same concepts as our grocery store example, but instead they deal with financial assets.",
        "start": 5120,
        "end": 53250,
        "confidence": 0.9854958,
